# Site information architecture

## Main nav

Primary practice links only: **Works · About · CV**.

Do not add secondary surfaces (Collaborations / design-for-hire, Writing go-live, Maps, Blog mirrors, external profiles) to the main nav without an explicit request.

## Footer

Secondary and site-wide links live in the footer: Works, About, CV, Collaborations, plus external/professional links (email, GitHub, LinkedIn, Concordia, etc.) as already wired.

- **Maps** (`/maps`) — staged / not live yet: routes build, but stay out of the footer and sitemap (`noindex`) until go-live (satellite + trees + resettled; Mapbox needs `PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN`)
- **Collaborations** (`/collaborations`) → footer, not main nav (publication / web work for others + hire CTA)
- Keep the footer quiet — short labels, no link farm

## Writing

Long-form essays can live at `/writing/[slug]` before they appear in nav. Discoverability via CV (and later an index) is enough until the Writing SEO go-live checklist in `writing-seo.mdc` is done.

## Homepage brand

On the homepage, the site title always shows the full name **Adam Simms** — never the condensed **AS** treatment used elsewhere when space is tight.
